        <item>
            <title>3.23.1</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:43:37 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>228</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.23.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's New in 3.23.1</h2><ul></ul><p><strong>Improved</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor waits for a destination folder that is offline, such as a disconnected drive, and renames the files when it is back. Files changed while waiting are analyzed again.</li><li>Monitor skips files it can't read instead of stopping, and keeps retrying files on a share that drops for a moment.</li><li>Built-in templates name files more predictably, and rename rules that ask not to include a date or other part of the original name are followed.</li><li>Large batches are sent in smaller parts, so they no longer fail for being too big.</li><li>Text recognition in scanned documents waits longer on slower Macs before switching to a faster method.</li><li>Zush starts faster.</li></ul><p><strong>Fixed</strong></p><ul><li>A file that was moved or deleted before renaming is kept in the list with its result instead of failing the whole batch.</li><li>A Mac where Zush was reinstalled is recognized again instead of showing that it can't be verified.</li><li>iCloud Drive, Dropbox and Google Drive folders can be watched in the App Store version.</li><li>iCloud files that start downloading slowly are no longer reported as stuck.</li><li>Checkout no longer stops with an error when it takes longer to open.</li><li>More EPUB books can be read.</li><li>Local AI models in Ollama no longer get stuck repeating the same tags, and model loading errors are explained.</li><li>The welcome window no longer shows a gray strip at the bottom.</li></ul>
]]></description>
